# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 09: MISSED-CALL RULES

**Route:** `/mctb/setup/missed-call-rules` | **Wizard:** Setup Step 2 (spec 07)  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-09-MISSED-CALL-RULES.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–08

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Missed-call Rules (`/mctb/setup/missed-call-rules`, wizard step 2).

## Primary job

Define **which call outcomes** create canonical missed-call events — not consent, SMS content, forwarding, schedule, or eligibility.

```
Call outcome matches enabled rule → MissedCallEvent → central eligibility engine
```

## Page scope

**Owns:** trigger conditions (no answer, busy, unreachable, rejected/voicemail only if runtime supports), no-answer timing only if MCTB owns it

**Does not own:** forwarding, consent, sender, message text, business hours, voicemail greeting, cooldown/max sends (→ Follow-up Rules), opt-out policy

## UI model

**Wizard:** one simple screen — checkboxes + plain-language helpers → Continue (persist before advance)

**Post-setup:** direct editor, Save changes, no stepper

**Defaults:** no answer / busy / unreachable on (operational — not consent attestation)

## Locked distinctions

- **Classification ≠ messaging eligibility** — no "text opted-out callers anyway"
- **Repeat calls** = separate events; cooldown is Follow-up Rules
- **Rules apply prospectively** — history not rewritten
- **Zero triggers** = validation error
- **Loading** — no false unchecked defaults

## Relationships

| Area | Relationship |
|------|----------------|
| Phone & Forwarding | Did call reach Transovo? |
| Missed-call Rules | Did outcome match enabled rule? |
| Consent / Schedule / Follow-up | After event created |

## Prohibited

Workflow builder, provider disposition codes, duplicate cooldown controls, fake triggers, rewriting history, mock controls

## Definition of done

See full spec §51 checklist.

